## Solution

We compute the ratio directly. With

$$r_n = \frac{\sqrt{n}}{n!}\left(\frac{n}{e}\right)^n,$$

we have

$$\frac{r_n}{r_{n+1}} = \frac{\sqrt{n}}{n!}\left(\frac{n}{e}\right)^n \cdot \frac{(n+1)!}{\sqrt{n+1}}\left(\frac{e}{n+1}\right)^{n+1} = \frac{\sqrt{n}}{\sqrt{n+1}}\cdot e\cdot\left(\frac{n}{n+1}\right)^n.$$

Taking logarithms,

$$\log\frac{r_n}{r_{n+1}} = \frac{1}{2}\log\frac{n}{n+1} + 1 + n\log\frac{n}{n+1} = 1 - \left(n+\tfrac{1}{2}\right)\log\left(1+\tfrac{1}{n}\right).$$

Now expand $\log(1+1/n)$ for large $n$:

$$\log\left(1+\frac{1}{n}\right) = \frac{1}{n} - \frac{1}{2n^2} + \frac{1}{3n^3} - \frac{1}{4n^4} + \cdots.$$

Multiplying by $\left(n+\tfrac{1}{2}\right)$:

$$\left(n+\tfrac{1}{2}\right)\log\left(1+\tfrac{1}{n}\right) = 1 + \frac{1}{2n} - \frac{1}{2n} - \frac{1}{4n^2} + \frac{1}{3n^2} + \frac{1}{6n^3} - \frac{1}{4n^3} - \cdots$$

$$= 1 + \left(-\frac{1}{4}+\frac{1}{3}\right)\frac{1}{n^2} + \left(\frac{1}{6}-\frac{1}{4}\right)\frac{1}{n^3} + \cdots = 1 + \frac{1}{12n^2} - \frac{1}{12n^3} + \cdots.$$

Therefore

$$\log\frac{r_n}{r_{n+1}} = 1 - \left[1 + \frac{1}{12n^2} - \frac{1}{12n^3} + \cdots\right] = -\frac{1}{12n^2} + \frac{1}{12n^3} - \cdots.$$

Multiplying by $n^2$:

$$n^2\log\frac{r_n}{r_{n+1}} = -\frac{1}{12} + \frac{1}{12n} - \cdots \;\xrightarrow{n\to\infty}\; -\frac{1}{12}.$$

### PROOF COMPLETE
